subproblems.statement:
Let k, N' ∈ ℕ, let H : ℝ^k → ℝ^{N'} be any map, and let B ⊆ ℝ^k be a Borel set. Then there are Borel sets A_l ⊆ B (l ∈ ℕ), pairwise disjoint, and reals κ_l > 0 (l ∈ ℕ) such that:
(i) κ_l|a − a'| ≤ |H(a) − H(a')| for all a, a' ∈ A_l;
(ii) at every point a of every A_l, H is differentiable and its derivative DH(a) = fderiv ℝ H a is injective;
(iii) every u ∈ B at which H is differentiable with injective derivative DH(u) belongs to some A_l.
